h vertex’s edges in ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, and the search never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"goes back along the edge it arrived by, so a self-loop or a parallel pair is found.","type":"text"}],"title":"findCycle()"},"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cycles","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"Cycles"},"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles/GraphProtocols/Graph/girth()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"girth","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/graph\/girth()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The length of a shortest cycle, in edges: 1 when there is a self-loop, 2 when there is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair of parallel edges; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when the graph is acyclic."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/girth()","title":"girth()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directedView"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs a